/-
# The ray-class counting vocabulary: the cone count of a ray class

This file fixes the object on which the counting for the sharp equidistribution of the ideals in
the ray classes of a congruence subgroup is performed.

* `rayConeCount 𝔪 𝔡 X` — the number of generators `α` (lying in the fundamental cone) of the
  ideals in the ray class of `𝔡` modulo `CongSubgroup K 𝔪`, of norm `≤ X / N𝔡`: those are the
  `α ∈ 𝔡⁻¹`, `α ≠ 0`, with `mixedEmbedding α` in the fundamental cone, such that `u * α` is
  `IsCongElem K 𝔪` for some unit `u` of `𝓞 K`.

  Equivalently (`NK.NUV2.RouteB.RayCount.torsion_mul_rayClassCnt`), `torsionOrder K` times the
  number of ideals of `𝓞 K` which are coprime to the support of `𝔪`, lie in the ray class of `𝔡`
  and have norm `≤ X`.  (`rayClassCnt K 𝔪 𝔡 X` is
  `NK.NUV2.RouteB.rayClassCnt`, the same count with the coprimality and class conditions
  spelled out.)

* `unitCongSubgroup 𝔪` — the subgroup of units of `𝓞 K` generated by the units `u` with
  `IsCongElem K 𝔪 u`; the class of a principal ideal `(α)` is `1` in the ray class group exactly
  when `u * α` is `IsCongElem` for some unit `u`, and the admissible `u`'s form a coset of this
  subgroup.  Its (finite) index governs the counting.

The counting itself is a sum, over the cosets of `unitCongSubgroup 𝔪` in `O_K^×`, of lattice-point
counts in cosets of the lattice `𝔪 𝔡⁻¹`, cut out by the sign half-spaces of the corresponding
units; the lattice-point counts are provided with a power-saving error term by
`NK.NUV2.RouteB.Dict.latticeCosetCount_halfspaces_isBigO`.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.NK.NUV2.RouteB.RayModulus.Defs
import Submission.NK.NUV2.RouteB.RayModulus.classOfIdeal_eq_iff
import Submission.NK.NUV2.RouteB.NarrowCoset.narrowCosetCount
import Submission.NK.NUV2.RouteB.RayModulus.CosetCountDefs
import Submission.NK.NUV2.HeckeAnalytic.Transfer
-- PORT435-BEGIN (v4.35 isDefEq respectTransparency compat)
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false
-- PORT435-END

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000

open NumberField IsDedekindDomain
open scoped Classical nonZeroDivisors NumberField

noncomputable section

namespace NK.NUV2.RouteB.RayCount

open NK.NUV2.RouteB

variable {K : Type} [Field K] [NumberField K]

/-- The subgroup of units of `𝓞 K` generated by those units `u` with `IsCongElem K 𝔪 u`: units
congruent to `1` modulo `𝔪` at the primes of the support, and positive at the real places of
`𝔪.pos`. -/
def unitCongSubgroup (𝔪 : Modulus K) : Subgroup (𝓞 K)ˣ :=
  Subgroup.closure {u : (𝓞 K)ˣ | IsCongElem K 𝔪 ((u : 𝓞 K) : K)}

/-- **The cone count of the ray class of `𝔡`.**  The number of generators `α` (in the fundamental
cone) of the ideals in the ray class of `𝔡` modulo `CongSubgroup K 𝔪`, of norm `≤ X / N𝔡`. -/
def rayConeCount (𝔪 : Modulus K) (𝔡 : (Ideal (𝓞 K))⁰) (X : ℝ) : ℕ :=
  Nat.card {α : K //
    α ∈ (((FractionalIdeal.mk0 K 𝔡)⁻¹ : (FractionalIdeal (𝓞 K)⁰ K)ˣ) :
      FractionalIdeal (𝓞 K)⁰ K) ∧
    α ≠ 0 ∧
    mixedEmbedding K α ∈ NumberField.mixedEmbedding.fundamentalCone K ∧
    (∃ u : (𝓞 K)ˣ, IsCongElem K 𝔪 (((u : 𝓞 K) : K) * α)) ∧
    mixedEmbedding.norm (mixedEmbedding K α) * (Ideal.absNorm (𝔡 : Ideal (𝓞 K)) : ℝ) ≤ X}

end NK.NUV2.RouteB.RayCount
